# Phase 4 — "leave it running". Written 2026-08-27 for the first unattended run.
#
# Parked on 466.0 rather than rotating. Phase 4 is a stability and threshold
# gate, and the band-switching trap in docs/bench-bringup.md is documented but
# unverified — a retune that carries noise-floor state across bands produces a
# burst of false detections after every switch. That is a variable worth adding
# only when somebody is watching. 466 is also the band the survey exists for.
#
# 10 MSPS deliberately, despite Gate 2 not being passed at that rate. The point
# of a long run is to find out what the overflow rate actually is under real
# diurnal load, which no bench measurement can tell us. Gain and ppm come from
# the profile: 39 and 0.64, both measured 2026-08-27.
#
# Audio capture on. 12000 events/hour at ~16 kB/s of traffic is roughly 2.3 GB
# a day, so 40 GB is about two and a half weeks; the budget stops capture and
# lets logging continue, so overrunning it costs audio, never events. Disk is
# 435 GB free. This is what lets the periodic emitters on 461-470 be identified
# offline instead of guessed at.
#
# Its own database, not data/survey.sqlite — that one holds the synthetic
# fixture scenario the test suite depends on.
RFSURVEY_DB=data/phase4.sqlite
RFSURVEY_ARGS=--freq 466.0e6 --rate 10e6 --capture-dir data/captures --capture-mb 40000
